We do the same, we just pull cash from the shopkeeps purse each cycle.

The real objective isn't the credit. The real objective is to get all
the shopkeeps cash. The only way to do that is to sell stuff. Credit
cloning has three essential components.

1. Convert your cash to credit and buy on credit.
2. Sell items to the shopkeep and get his (her?) cash.
3. Have pet steal money from floor to convert shopkeeps cash to yours.

It goes faster as you pile more money on the floor. So doing the
sales cycle while the pet steals creates more cash flow than doing it
afterwards.

In fact I usually enter a shop alone and leave the pet outside to get
set up. I'll pick up and price ID every item. Then I'll pile them all
in a far corner. I then drop a cursed item on it so that the pet will
leave the pile alone. I'll sell whatever I own that the shopkeep will
buy to get more cash. I'll then sell cycle until I have no cash (it's
on the floor) and no credit. Then and only then will I let the pet it.

And as I'm sure you know, don't sell tripe! Keep it in your pack to give
to the pet.


